# lecturer observes that students’ examination marks approximately follow a normal 
distribution with a mean of 70 and a standard deviation of 10. 
Write a Python program to calculate the probability that a randomly selected student scores 
between 60 and 80, and to plot the normal distribution with the interval highlighted.





from scipy.stats import norm

p = norm.cdf(80,70,10) - norm.cdf(60,70,10)
print("Probability:", p)
